# Every file is checked out byte for byte as committed, on Windows too:
# tests compare exact bytes (recordings, conformance tables, expected
# output), and a CRLF checkout would change them.
* -text
# Recorded terminal output and fuzz seeds are bytes, not text to tidy.
bench/payloads/** -whitespace
fux-vt/fuzz/seeds/** binary
# The conformance table is tab-separated, and a row's last columns may be
# empty.
fux-vt/tests/data/conformance.txt -whitespace
